(6672890, 997686, 43463, '<td valign="top">Floral rays slowly open one by one<br/>yellow bursts with the touch of the sun.<br/>The fields come alive with morning light<br/>as bugs &amp; plants shake of the blanket of night.<br/> <br/>Wow, very bold, and vibrant hues of green and yellow! I also love all the detail in the sunflower.</td>', 'Floral rays slowly open one by oneyellow bursts with the touch of the sun.The fields come alive with morning lightas bugs & plants shake of the blanket of night. Wow, very bold, and vibrant hues of green and yellow! I also love all the detail in the sunflower.', '2012-02-12 13:37:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(6672899, 997862, 43463, '<td valign="top">"I wouldn''t venture to far beyond these woods," warned Cooper.<br/>"And why is that," Warren asked warily as he slung his bow on his back. He had just spotted the stag he had been tracking off in the distance.<br/>"Notice how that part of the forest is darker than where we stand? Well, long ago they say a witch was cleaved to a tree. Her evil spirit remains and any who venture to close," Cooper extended his hands, wiggled his fingers, and made a loud, slurping sound, "she sucks yer soul out. The last thing you see as you are being drawn in is the faces of the others she trapped. They call that tree, the Soul Catcher."<br/>Warren wrinkled his face in disgust and shook his head, "Do you really believe that crap? Well you stay here then, I''ll bring home the venison tonight." <br/>Cooper watched Warren rush forward and disappear in the deeper reaches of the forest. "Somehow, I doubt that," he shook his head sadly.<br/> <br/> <br/>Very spooky and surreal photo! It makes me think this is a cover page to a book with spooky stories. The B&amp;W is perfect for it adds to the eeriness of the scene.</td>', '"I wouldn''t venture to far beyond these woods," warned Cooper."And why is that," Warren asked warily as he slung his bow on his back. He had just spotted the stag he had been tracking off in the distance."Notice how that part of the forest is darker than where we stand? Well, long ago they say a witch was cleaved to a tree. Her evil spirit remains and any who venture to close," Cooper extended his hands, wiggled his fingers, and made a loud, slurping sound, "she sucks yer soul out. The last thing you see as you are being drawn in is the faces of the others she trapped. They call that tree, the Soul Catcher."Warren wrinkled his face in disgust and shook his head, "Do you really believe that crap? Well you stay here then, I''ll bring home the venison tonight." Cooper watched Warren rush forward and disappear in the deeper reaches of the forest. "Somehow, I doubt that," he shook his head sadly.  Very spooky and surreal photo! It makes me think this is a cover page to a book with spooky stories. The B&W is perfect for it adds to the eeriness of the scene.', '2012-02-12 13:59:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(6672901, 995223, 15711, '<td valign="top">I may have told you this before but Huntington has a special place in my heart.  My Dad was a lifeguard there after WWII.  Every time I see the pier or a lifeguard stand, I think of him.  Thanks for a happy remembrance. 7</td>', 'I may have told you this before but Huntington has a special place in my heart.  My Dad was a lifeguard there after WWII.  Every time I see the pier or a lifeguard stand, I think of him.  Thanks for a happy remembrance. 7', '2012-02-12 14:01:11.000000', NULL, 1),
