(6676540, 993927, 30214, '<td valign="top">beautiful portrait. The exposure is top-notch</td>', 'beautiful portrait. The exposure is top-notch', '2012-02-14 14:45:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(6676571, 997554, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Well, I know this is you - but even if I didn''t, who else could it be? Truly one of those pictures that make the rest of us look a bit silly - masterful in every sense. I have to say before you put this image up my favourite image on DPC was one of <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=35804" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">RKT</a>''s:<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=810703" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1060/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_810703.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1060/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_810703.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1060/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_810703.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>It''s 3 year reign is now ended. Sorry Rachel (though I have a feeling she won''t mind one bit).<br/> <br/>So, why do I like it so much? I wish I knew, but I suspect it''s about the juxtapositions - visible water where it''s dry, none where we know it is wet, low contrast below, high above, sharpness without clarity above, softness with clarity below; then of course there are the absent heads and the great puzzles of ''where are they?'' and ''where are you?'' when you are taking the shot. But most of all the parasols looking like umbrellas against the rain you have created for us - a storm perhaps; one that the voyager and his servant are blissfully unaware as they cruise serenely and without a care (for they have not the apparatus to support such thought) as they make their way through the protective realm of the sea.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I wouldn''t dare.<br/> <br/>Overall: Spectacular - 10 of course.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Well, I know this is you - but even if I didn''t, who else could it be? Truly one of those pictures that make the rest of us look a bit silly - masterful in every sense. I have to say before you put this image up my favourite image on DPC was one of  RKT''s:   It''s 3 year reign is now ended. Sorry Rachel (though I have a feeling she won''t mind one bit). So, why do I like it so much? I wish I knew, but I suspect it''s about the juxtapositions - visible water where it''s dry, none where we know it is wet, low contrast below, high above, sharpness without clarity above, softness with clarity below; then of course there are the absent heads and the great puzzles of ''where are they?'' and ''where are you?'' when you are taking the shot. But most of all the parasols looking like umbrellas against the rain you have created for us - a storm perhaps; one that the voyager and his servant are blissfully unaware as they cruise serenely and without a care (for they have not the apparatus to support such thought) as they make their way through the protective realm of the sea. Critical stuff: I wouldn''t dare. Overall: Spectacular - 10 of course.', '2012-02-14 15:54:15.000000', NULL, 1),
