(6677229, 996226, 34547, '<td valign="top">Wow, not swarming with tourists! Beautiful colors and contrast. Is it leaning a little left?</td>', 'Wow, not swarming with tourists! Beautiful colors and contrast. Is it leaning a little left?', '2012-02-15 02:27:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(6677230, 996255, 34547, '<td valign="top">Neat perspective but way too processed looking.</td>', 'Neat perspective but way too processed looking.', '2012-02-15 02:28:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(6677231, 995975, 30364, '<td valign="top">It''s a silly-serious portrait, which is one of my favourite things.  But it''s a healthy cut above other silly-serious portraits for a few reasons.  <br/> <br/>First is the deadpan expression ... not a simulated deadpan, a real one.  First-and-a-half is the distortion to the features caused by the goggles, and the fact that he is apparently oblivious or indifferent to it.  Second is the orientation in landscape, which complements his splendidly landscaped ears.  Third is the beautiful craftsmanship evident in the technical quality of the photograph.  And last but best of all is the fact that it is a <i>joyful</i> photograph, but without any explicit joy being visible.  You have here the <i>implicit</i> joy of two things:  Photography, and Family (I am assuming the family part, but it''s really gotta be I reckon).  <br/> <br/>This is what photographs and photography are really about.  10, and a heartfelt Order of the Thumb.  Thank you.<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=800078" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg"/></a></td>', 'It''s a silly-serious portrait, which is one of my favourite things.  But it''s a healthy cut above other silly-serious portraits for a few reasons.   First is the deadpan expression ... not a simulated deadpan, a real one.  First-and-a-half is the distortion to the features caused by the goggles, and the fact that he is apparently oblivious or indifferent to it.  Second is the orientation in landscape, which complements his splendidly landscaped ears.  Third is the beautiful craftsmanship evident in the technical quality of the photograph.  And last but best of all is the fact that it is a joyful photograph, but without any explicit joy being visible.  You have here the implicit joy of two things:  Photography, and Family (I am assuming the family part, but it''s really gotta be I reckon).   This is what photographs and photography are really about.  10, and a heartfelt Order of the Thumb.  Thank you.', '2012-02-15 02:29:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(6677232, 996905, 34547, '<td valign="top">Very classic and sensual. Her pose and the vignetting drive your eyes right into hers. Beautifully done.</td>', 'Very classic and sensual. Her pose and the vignetting drive your eyes right into hers. Beautifully done.', '2012-02-15 02:30:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(6677233, 996316, 34547, '<td valign="top">COOL! Looks under-exposed but I like the framing and grayness of the elephant against so much color.</td>', 'COOL! Looks under-exposed but I like the framing and grayness of the elephant against so much color.', '2012-02-15 02:32:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(6677234, 996015, 93565, '<td valign="top">The processing is a bit over the top, in a lot of ways, but I think the end product is very cool This has taken on a look entirely different from simply a normal macro of a katydid, bordering instead on an interesting rendering of a character from a pixar film or something. Pretty cool shot.</td>', 'The processing is a bit over the top, in a lot of ways, but I think the end product is very cool This has taken on a look entirely different from simply a normal macro of a katydid, bordering instead on an interesting rendering of a character from a pixar film or something. Pretty cool shot.', '2012-02-15 02:33:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(6677235, 994783, 30364, '<td valign="top">A <i>literally</i> magical photograph; it''s enchanting.  10 &amp; thank you, and this thing ....<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=800078" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg"/></a></td>', 'A literally magical photograph; it''s enchanting.  10 & thank you, and this thing ....', '2012-02-15 02:33:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(6677236, 996713, 34547, '<td valign="top">I guess the poor guy on the end doesn''t want to be in the picture. :(</td>', 'I guess the poor guy on the end doesn''t want to be in the picture. :(', '2012-02-15 02:34:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(6677237, 997101, 34547, '<td valign="top">A lot of distracting elements, in my opinion, taking away from the neat architecture and colors.</td>', 'A lot of distracting elements, in my opinion, taking away from the neat architecture and colors.', '2012-02-15 02:36:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(6677239, 995870, 34547, '<td valign="top">Well captured but I think I''ve seen this way too many times. Nonetheless, I think I''ll have to try it one day. :)</td>', 'Well captured but I think I''ve seen this way too many times. Nonetheless, I think I''ll have to try it one day. :)', '2012-02-15 02:38:48.000000', NULL, 1);
