(6688880, 994628, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: This is an amazing portrait Lev - more so given the original file; I can''t remember where I saw that, but to have seen the potential and then to pull off an edit to this effect is amazing. Toning and structure is just brilliant and the expression of the women priceless.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I think the linearly textured background over her left shoulder is perhaps a little distracting - might it have been selectively blurred? (Nit-picking!)<br/> <br/>Overall: A magnificent portrait - very well seen and masterfully edited.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: This is an amazing portrait Lev - more so given the original file; I can''t remember where I saw that, but to have seen the potential and then to pull off an edit to this effect is amazing. Toning and structure is just brilliant and the expression of the women priceless. Critical stuff: I think the linearly textured background over her left shoulder is perhaps a little distracting - might it have been selectively blurred? (Nit-picking!) Overall: A magnificent portrait - very well seen and masterfully edited.', '2012-02-23 16:19:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(6688881, 997695, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: This is the third time I''ve typed out a long comment (lost it twice!) - let''s try again. Not that I''m particularly familiar with you from this angle, I''m pretty convinced this is a <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=113278" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">MinsoPhoto</a> self portrait. I find the image to be bold, brave and mighty fine! I like the stark lighting and the deep shadows so provided, I like the skirting and how it shows us that corner in a way the walls do not, I like the white squiggle bottom left and the textures of the surfaces and I very much like the ceiling vent and how that tames the space. Fantastic contrast too.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nope.<br/> <br/>Overall: Bravo. I could see this hanging in a gallery - and this coming from someone who shoots very different nudes. I''ve given you a 9 - in lesser challenges I may have gone higher but for this one I''m reserving my 10s for just four shots that have knocked my socks off.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: This is the third time I''ve typed out a long comment (lost it twice!) - let''s try again. Not that I''m particularly familiar with you from this angle, I''m pretty convinced this is a  MinsoPhoto self portrait. I find the image to be bold, brave and mighty fine! I like the stark lighting and the deep shadows so provided, I like the skirting and how it shows us that corner in a way the walls do not, I like the white squiggle bottom left and the textures of the surfaces and I very much like the ceiling vent and how that tames the space. Fantastic contrast too. Critical stuff: Nope. Overall: Bravo. I could see this hanging in a gallery - and this coming from someone who shoots very different nudes. I''ve given you a 9 - in lesser challenges I may have gone higher but for this one I''m reserving my 10s for just four shots that have knocked my socks off.', '2012-02-23 16:19:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(6688882, 998140, 74588, '<td valign="top">like it    9</td>', 'like it    9', '2012-02-23 16:19:50.000000', NULL, 1),
