(6688895, 997757, 76335, '<td valign="top">I love the velvety, gritty, muddy tones and textures.</td>', 'I love the velvety, gritty, muddy tones and textures.', '2012-02-23 16:25:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(6688896, 997480, 76335, '<td valign="top">Balanced tension. Beautiful.</td>', 'Balanced tension. Beautiful.', '2012-02-23 16:25:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(6688898, 997793, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I appreciate landscape photography but seldom do I enjoy one as much as this. The human element adds much and your tone-mapped presentation is a perfect match for the scene. The perspective offered by the trailer is supported so well by that long dark cloud above and this slight over-exposure does much to optimise the image.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: The slight blue handing around the central part of the clouds looks a little unfortunate against the rest of the image.<br/> <br/>Overall: Great stuff. Very enjoyable.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I appreciate landscape photography but seldom do I enjoy one as much as this. The human element adds much and your tone-mapped presentation is a perfect match for the scene. The perspective offered by the trailer is supported so well by that long dark cloud above and this slight over-exposure does much to optimise the image. Critical stuff: The slight blue handing around the central part of the clouds looks a little unfortunate against the rest of the image. Overall: Great stuff. Very enjoyable.', '2012-02-23 16:28:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(6688901, 994088, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I like quirky portraits and this certainly hits that button. The slight coloration is absolutely perfect. The intensity of the eyes and the wild hair stops you in your tracks. Some may complain about the stray hair over the eye - I really like that, it communicates spontaneity.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I think main part of the hair looks over sharpened/defined - a low opacity blur brush may have helped to dispel some of its ''crunchiness''.<br/> <br/>Overall: Unusual and compelling portrait.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I like quirky portraits and this certainly hits that button. The slight coloration is absolutely perfect. The intensity of the eyes and the wild hair stops you in your tracks. Some may complain about the stray hair over the eye - I really like that, it communicates spontaneity. Critical stuff: I think main part of the hair looks over sharpened/defined - a low opacity blur brush may have helped to dispel some of its ''crunchiness''. Overall: Unusual and compelling portrait.', '2012-02-23 16:32:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(6688908, 994471, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Johanna - I love quirky portraits and you are the master of those. This is just superb. The humour, the matter-of-factness, the seemingly relaxed chicken are of course the stars, but the technicals are also compelling - the nicely diffused background, the shadow on the face and the well-preserved reflection in the table - all contribute much.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Although the shadow is great on Carl''s face and on the bird - I think it is perhaps a bit deep on his right hand.<br/> <br/>Overall: A portrait of the highest quality.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Johanna - I love quirky portraits and you are the master of those. This is just superb. The humour, the matter-of-factness, the seemingly relaxed chicken are of course the stars, but the technicals are also compelling - the nicely diffused background, the shadow on the face and the well-preserved reflection in the table - all contribute much. Critical stuff: Although the shadow is great on Carl''s face and on the bird - I think it is perhaps a bit deep on his right hand. Overall: A portrait of the highest quality.', '2012-02-23 16:39:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(6688909, 997776, 44611, '<td valign="top">This is a bit like a Lowry painting.  I love the composition and all the colourful activity.  It''s different and fun.</td>', 'This is a bit like a Lowry painting.  I love the composition and all the colourful activity.  It''s different and fun.', '2012-02-23 16:39:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(6688910, 997676, 100393, '<td valign="top">This is a beautifully rendered image - brave to offer up a monochrome despite the rig colours available to you. It works very well though.<br/> <br/>Great stuff.</td>', 'This is a beautifully rendered image - brave to offer up a monochrome despite the rig colours available to you. It works very well though. Great stuff.', '2012-02-23 16:40:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(6688911, 998196, 105466, '<td valign="top">I feel the cigarett is too white in this otherwise beautifully warm toned portrait.</td>', 'I feel the cigarett is too white in this otherwise beautifully warm toned portrait.', '2012-02-23 16:40:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6688919, 993778, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Well, you have stopped me for long enough to drop one of these comments upon you and I DO like the fact that you have challenged us with this image... Now that you have me, I find the eye fascinating  - like a glimpse of ET frozen in a stasis chamber!<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I find the colour noise ugly and all though the image is somewhat compelling, it is nonetheless difficult to like.<br/> <br/>Overall: Always pleased to see people sticking challenging images into Free Studies so thanks for that.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Well, you have stopped me for long enough to drop one of these comments upon you and I DO like the fact that you have challenged us with this image... Now that you have me, I find the eye fascinating  - like a glimpse of ET frozen in a stasis chamber! Critical stuff: I find the colour noise ugly and all though the image is somewhat compelling, it is nonetheless difficult to like. Overall: Always pleased to see people sticking challenging images into Free Studies so thanks for that.', '2012-02-23 16:48:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(6688925, 997137, 91342, '<td valign="top">I''d crop a bit off the top.</td>', 'I''d crop a bit off the top.', '2012-02-23 16:54:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(6688926, 997840, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I don''t really understand this image and I enjoy how another part of my brain asks me why I expect to. I do quite like the colour palette too....<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Despite the internal dialogue this image promotes, I''m not a fan - even as an abstract I feel the image isn''t effective for me - I think I''d have enjoyed lower contrast and higher saturation.<br/> <br/>Overall: A challenging piece of work but not one for me I''m afraid.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I don''t really understand this image and I enjoy how another part of my brain asks me why I expect to. I do quite like the colour palette too.... Critical stuff: Despite the internal dialogue this image promotes, I''m not a fan - even as an abstract I feel the image isn''t effective for me - I think I''d have enjoyed lower contrast and higher saturation. Overall: A challenging piece of work but not one for me I''m afraid.', '2012-02-23 16:55:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(6688929, 996073, 100393, '<td valign="top">Lovely capture and a nicely dark presentation. Great clarity where it needs to be.</td>', 'Lovely capture and a nicely dark presentation. Great clarity where it needs to be.', '2012-02-23 16:58:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(6688933, 996979, 91342, '<td valign="top">Crop the top off.</td>', 'Crop the top off.', '2012-02-23 17:00:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(6688940, 993597, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Despite the excellent pigeon, it''s the background I find most interesting - it''s so very cornery! and with the subliminal suggestion of a face peering through the blur. The slight coloration works really well and the movement blur adds an uncommon thick softness to the image - like a visual muffle.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Some additional grain may have contributed to the mood.<br/> <br/>Overall: If you are going to make a blurry pigeon - this is the way to do it.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Despite the excellent pigeon, it''s the background I find most interesting - it''s so very cornery! and with the subliminal suggestion of a face peering through the blur. The slight coloration works really well and the movement blur adds an uncommon thick softness to the image - like a visual muffle. Critical stuff: Some additional grain may have contributed to the mood. Overall: If you are going to make a blurry pigeon - this is the way to do it.', '2012-02-23 17:10:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(6688947, 997650, 100393, '<td valign="top">John - these scenes are always really compelling but here, strangely, it is that breaking wave rather than the fishermen that draws my interest - not a bad thing, but unexpected.The bird is surprisingly prominent too. The glowy rendition reflects your work and once again you have judged it well. My brain tells me the men are over sharpened but my eyes don''t reveal much when I scrutinise closely.<br/> <br/>Great scene - well made.</td>', 'John - these scenes are always really compelling but here, strangely, it is that breaking wave rather than the fishermen that draws my interest - not a bad thing, but unexpected.The bird is surprisingly prominent too. The glowy rendition reflects your work and once again you have judged it well. My brain tells me the men are over sharpened but my eyes don''t reveal much when I scrutinise closely. Great scene - well made.', '2012-02-23 17:16:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(6688958, 994863, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I love these abandoned buildings shots and this is a nice one. The floor tiles work really well in offering a sense of depth and you choice of viewpoint is just right. I also really like how my brain can''t decide whether this is a monochrome image or just very drab. The vignette is excellent too.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Not really<br/> <br/>Overall: Nicely done.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I love these abandoned buildings shots and this is a nice one. The floor tiles work really well in offering a sense of depth and you choice of viewpoint is just right. I also really like how my brain can''t decide whether this is a monochrome image or just very drab. The vignette is excellent too. Critical stuff: Not really Overall: Nicely done.', '2012-02-23 17:23:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(6688963, 996060, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: This is a highly interesting image with a most novel POV. The overall composition is quite immersive - we feel pulled in. I like the grain and the toning and the eye contact with the subject works really well as a secondary hook after the flick itself.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: The vertical banding to the right of the hand.<br/> <br/>Overall: Bold and thought provoking. Excellent.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: This is a highly interesting image with a most novel POV. The overall composition is quite immersive - we feel pulled in. I like the grain and the toning and the eye contact with the subject works really well as a secondary hook after the flick itself. Critical stuff: The vertical banding to the right of the hand. Overall: Bold and thought provoking. Excellent.', '2012-02-23 17:26:39.000000', NULL, 1),
