(6691412, 997123, 18197, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mike_311:</b></div><hr/><i> like i commented to someone else. this is a snapshot of someones elses art, you need to add your own spin to it to make it an interesting picture to me.<br/> <br/>perspective, better composition, adding some other subject (like a bird, for instance) or even make the lighting itself the subject. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I''ve seen this comment from you before on a number of photos. In this particular case I think it under-appreciates some of the challenges of night photography and in fact, if this is successful at all, it is because of composition, perspective, lighting. Time to raise your own game, IMO.</td>', 'Originally posted by mike_311: like i commented to someone else. this is a snapshot of someones elses art, you need to add your own spin to it to make it an interesting picture to me. perspective, better composition, adding some other subject (like a bird, for instance) or even make the lighting itself the subject.   I''ve seen this comment from you before on a number of photos. In this particular case I think it under-appreciates some of the challenges of night photography and in fact, if this is successful at all, it is because of composition, perspective, lighting. Time to raise your own game, IMO.', '2012-02-25 00:09:40.000000', NULL, 0),
